Election specific information for the November 3, 2026 election; including important dates, polling locations, wait time maps, sample ballots, reports, and live streaming. 

## Tuesday, November 3, 2026  
Joint general & Special Election

Last Day to Register to Vote: Monday, October 5, 2026  
 Last Day to Apply for Ballot By Mail: Friday, October 23, 2026  
 Early Voting Starts: Monday, October 19, 2026  
 Early Voting Ends: Friday, October 30, 2026  
 Election Day: Tuesday, November 3, 2026  

Click each heading below to view resources and information about the current election.

 Polling Locations  Wait Times  Sample Ballots  Limited Ballot  Reports  Live Streaming 

## Early Voting Locations

**Note: You may vote at any Polling Site in Travis County.**

**Date and Time:**Monday, October 19th – Friday, October 30th, 2026 (7am-7pm)

*Some locations will have extended hours on the last two days of Early Voting*

[Download Early Voting Polling Sites PDF](https://votetravis.gov/wp-content/uploads/G26-Early-Voting-Flyer-9.21.pdf)

## Election Day Locations

**Note:****You may vote at any Polling Site in Travis County.**

**Date and Time:**Tuesday, November 3, 2026 (7am-7pm)

[Download Election Day Polling Sites PDF](https://votetravis.gov/wp-content/uploads/G26-Election-Day-Flyer-FINAL-Website-wNotice.pdf)

**Sample Ballots Coming Soon**

**Click**[November 3rd, 2026 Consolidated Ballot](https://votetravis.gov/wp-content/uploads/G26-Bedsheet-Ballot-Corrected-Final2.pdf)**to view all eligible contests in the November Election.**

**Click [Voter Lookup](https://votetravis.gov/voter-lookup/#VoterEligibilitySearch) to view your voter registration status and personalized ballot.**

**Click [Accessible Ballot](https://tx.omniballot.us/sites/48453/default/app/home) to view your interactive personal ballot.**

## [Have You Moved Here from Another Texas County and Want to Vote?​](https://votetravis.gov/current-election-information/current-election/)

A registered voter who has moved from the county in which he or she is registered, to a new county of residence in Texas, and who will not be registered to vote in the new county on or before Election Day, may be eligible to vote a “limited ballot.” Limited ballots may be voted in person or by mail in the new county of residence in the upcoming Election under the following conditions:

*   The person seeking to vote a limited ballot would be eligible to vote in the former county of residence on election day if still residing there;  
*   The person seeking to vote a limited ballot is registered to vote in the former county of residence at the time the person (1) offers to vote in the new county of residence or (2) applies for registration in the new county; and
*   The person’s voter registration is not effective in the new county of residence on or before election day

Limited Ballots are available ONLY during the Early Voting period for the upcoming election at 5501 Airport Blvd, Austin, Texas 78751. If you believe you are qualified to vote a limited ballot, please call (512) 238-8683 to confirm your eligibility. You may visit the [Texas Secretary of State’s website](https://www.sos.state.tx.us/) for more information about limited ballot voting in Texas.[Limited Ballot Voters and District Chart (Chapters 111 and 112, Texas Election Code)](https://www.sos.state.tx.us/elections/laws/advisory2022-29.shtml)

**November 3, 2026 Election**[Live Turnout Tracker](https://updates.electionlink.net/widgets/travistx/2026-11-03/index.html)*Travis County contains 308 precincts. The Live Turnout Tracker only reflects the 299 precincts with Active voters in the November 3, 2026, Election. The Voter Registration total as of 10/18/2026 is 948,575.

